{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.Knot.MortonFranksWilliams","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.Knot.MortonFranksWilliams","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:Mathlib.Tactic.Linarith"],"declarations":28,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Knot.MortonFranksWilliams.sixOne_torusFourFive_same_spread","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Knot.MortonFranksWilliams.sixOne_torusFourFive_same_spread","kind":"theorem","line":257,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Knot/MortonFranksWilliams.lean#L257-L262","doc":"The two witnesses have **equal spread but disjoint degree windows** —\n`[-2, 4]` against `[12, 18]`. MFW reads only the spread, which is why both\ngive `4` while the polynomials themselves are nothing alike. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Knot.MortonFranksWilliams.torusFourFive_not_three_strand","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Knot.MortonFranksWilliams.torusFourFive_not_three_strand","kind":"theorem","line":249,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Knot/MortonFranksWilliams.lean#L249-L255","doc":"**The separation is not special to `6₁`.** No 3-strand braid closes to a\nlink with `T(4,5)`'s degree window either, so the bound genuinely distinguishes\n`4` from `3` on a knot whose braid index is fixed by a theorem rather than by\nthe computation under test. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Knot.MortonFranksWilliams.torusFourFive_tight","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Knot.MortonFranksWilliams.torusFourFive_tight","kind":"theorem","line":244,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Knot/MortonFranksWilliams.lean#L244-L247","doc":"`T(4,5)`'s window is tight on both sides, exactly as `6₁`'s is. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Knot.MortonFranksWilliams.torusFourFive","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Knot.MortonFranksWilliams.torusFourFive","kind":"def","line":232,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Knot/MortonFranksWilliams.lean#L232-L242","doc":"The measured MFW input for the torus knot `T(4,5)`: HOMFLY `v`-degree\nwindow `[12, 18]` on the 4-strand word `(σ₁σ₂σ₃)⁵`, writhe `15`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Knot.MortonFranksWilliams.sixOne_four_le_strands","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Knot.MortonFranksWilliams.sixOne_four_le_strands","kind":"theorem","line":214,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Knot/MortonFranksWilliams.lean#L214-L220","doc":"**Every representative of `6₁` needs at least 4 strands.** Together with the\ncomputed 4-strand closure cited above, the braid index of `6₁` is exactly `4`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Knot.MortonFranksWilliams.sixOne_not_three_strand","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Knot.MortonFranksWilliams.sixOne_not_three_strand","kind":"theorem","line":204,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Knot/MortonFranksWilliams.lean#L204-L212","doc":"**No 3-strand braid closes to a link with `6₁`'s HOMFLY degree window.**\nThis is the step that separates `4` from `3`. Among the *tabulated* knots the\nproducer checks, none tests that separation — `3₁`, `4₁`, `5₁`, `5₂`, `6₂`, `6₃`\nall have braid index `2` or `3` — so the discrimination is exercised\nindependently by `torusFourFive` below rather than only on the knot under\ntest. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Knot.MortonFranksWilliams.sixOne_tight","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Knot.MortonFranksWilliams.sixOne_tight","kind":"theorem","line":199,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Knot/MortonFranksWilliams.lean#L199-L202","doc":"The MFW window for `6₁` is **tight on both sides**: the derived bound\n`spread + 2 ≤ 2n` holds with equality at `n = 4`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Knot.MortonFranksWilliams.sixOne","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Knot.MortonFranksWilliams.sixOne","kind":"def","line":187,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Knot/MortonFranksWilliams.lean#L187-L197","doc":"The measured MFW input for `6₁`: HOMFLY `v`-degree window `[-2, 4]`, and the\n4-strand representative of writhe `1`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Knot.MortonFranksWilliams.rep_unbounded","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Knot.MortonFranksWilliams.rep_unbounded","kind":"theorem","line":158,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Knot/MortonFranksWilliams.lean#L158-L166","doc":"**Hence there is no maximal braid index**: the representable strand numbers\nare unbounded above, so `max` is `∞` for every link and carries no information.\nThe braid index is a MINIMUM precisely because this maximum is degenerate. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Knot.MortonFranksWilliams.rep_upward","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Knot.MortonFranksWilliams.rep_upward","kind":"theorem","line":151,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Knot/MortonFranksWilliams.lean#L151-L156","doc":"Representability is **upward closed** under stabilisation. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Knot.MortonFranksWilliams.Markov.stab","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Knot.MortonFranksWilliams.Markov.stab","kind":"theorem","line":147,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Knot/MortonFranksWilliams.lean#L147-L147","doc":"stabilisation adds a strand without changing the closure ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Knot.MortonFranksWilliams.Markov.mk","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Knot.MortonFranksWilliams.Markov.mk","kind":"ctor","line":145,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Knot/MortonFranksWilliams.lean#L145-L145","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Knot.MortonFranksWilliams.Markov","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Knot.MortonFranksWilliams.Markov","kind":"class","line":142,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Knot/MortonFranksWilliams.lean#L142-L147","doc":"Markov stabilisation `β ↦ β·σₙ^{±1}` leaves the closure unchanged while\nadding a strand. Carried as a hypothesis on an abstract representability\npredicate: `Rep n` reads \"some braid on `n` strands closes to this link\". ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Knot.MortonFranksWilliams.no_representative_of_spread_gt","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Knot.MortonFranksWilliams.no_representative_of_spread_gt","kind":"theorem","line":131,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Knot/MortonFranksWilliams.lean#L131-L138","doc":"**The contrapositive — the form that actually rules a strand number out.**\nIf the HOMFLY degree spread is too wide for `n` strands, then no braid on `n`\nstrands closes to that link. This is how MFW is used in practice. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Knot.MortonFranksWilliams.MFWWitness.writhe_bounds","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Knot.MortonFranksWilliams.MFWWitness.writhe_bounds","kind":"theorem","line":119,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Knot/MortonFranksWilliams.lean#L119-L127","doc":"Adding (1) and (2) instead constrains the **writhe** at fixed `n`. Stated as\na two-sided pair rather than with `|·|` to keep the import surface minimal. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Knot.MortonFranksWilliams.MFWWitness.selfLinking_le","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Knot.MortonFranksWilliams.MFWWitness.selfLinking_le","kind":"theorem","line":111,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Knot/MortonFranksWilliams.lean#L111-L117","doc":"**Reading MFW (1) alone bounds a MAXIMUM.** The self-linking number of the\ntransverse representative is `sl = e − n`; the same trace that bounds the braid\nindex below bounds `sl` above. This is the HOMFLY sharpening of Bennequin's\n`sl ≤ 2g − 1`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Knot.MortonFranksWilliams.MFWWitness.braid_bound","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Knot.MortonFranksWilliams.MFWWitness.braid_bound","kind":"theorem","line":105,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Knot/MortonFranksWilliams.lean#L105-L109","doc":"**The MFW lower bound on the braid index**, division-free: any strand\nnumber admitting a representative satisfies `spread + 2 ≤ 2n`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Knot.MortonFranksWilliams.MFWWitness.spread_le_two_mul_sub_two","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Knot.MortonFranksWilliams.MFWWitness.spread_le_two_mul_sub_two","kind":"theorem","line":97,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Knot/MortonFranksWilliams.lean#L97-L103","doc":"**The crux: subtracting the two inequalities cancels the writhe.** `e` is\nnot a link invariant while the degree window is, so only the difference is\nusable. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Knot.MortonFranksWilliams.MFWWitness.dmin_le_dmax","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Knot.MortonFranksWilliams.MFWWitness.dmin_le_dmax","kind":"theorem","line":91,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Knot/MortonFranksWilliams.lean#L91-L91","doc":"the degree window is non-empty (`mindeg ≤ maxdeg` for a nonzero HOMFLY).\nNeeded for `writhe_bounds`; NOT derivable from the MFW pair alone, so it is\ncarried explicitly rather than quietly assumed. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Knot.MortonFranksWilliams.MFWWitness.mfw_upper","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Knot.MortonFranksWilliams.MFWWitness.mfw_upper","kind":"theorem","line":87,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Knot/MortonFranksWilliams.lean#L87-L87","doc":"MFW (2) ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Knot.MortonFranksWilliams.MFWWitness.mfw_lower","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Knot.MortonFranksWilliams.MFWWitness.mfw_lower","kind":"theorem","line":85,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Knot/MortonFranksWilliams.lean#L85-L85","doc":"MFW (1) ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Knot.MortonFranksWilliams.MFWWitness.one_le_n","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Knot.MortonFranksWilliams.MFWWitness.one_le_n","kind":"theorem","line":83,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Knot/MortonFranksWilliams.lean#L83-L83","doc":"a braid has at least one strand ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Knot.MortonFranksWilliams.MFWWitness.dmax","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Knot.MortonFranksWilliams.MFWWitness.dmax","kind":"def","line":81,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Knot/MortonFranksWilliams.lean#L81-L81","doc":"`maxdeg_v` of the HOMFLY polynomial of the closure ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Knot.MortonFranksWilliams.MFWWitness.dmin","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Knot.MortonFranksWilliams.MFWWitness.dmin","kind":"def","line":79,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Knot/MortonFranksWilliams.lean#L79-L79","doc":"`mindeg_v` of the HOMFLY polynomial of the closure ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Knot.MortonFranksWilliams.MFWWitness.e","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Knot.MortonFranksWilliams.MFWWitness.e","kind":"def","line":77,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Knot/MortonFranksWilliams.lean#L77-L77","doc":"exponent sum (writhe) of the braid word ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Knot.MortonFranksWilliams.MFWWitness.n","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Knot.MortonFranksWilliams.MFWWitness.n","kind":"def","line":75,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Knot/MortonFranksWilliams.lean#L75-L75","doc":"number of strands of the braid representative ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Knot.MortonFranksWilliams.MFWWitness.mk","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Knot.MortonFranksWilliams.MFWWitness.mk","kind":"ctor","line":73,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Knot/MortonFranksWilliams.lean#L73-L73","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Knot.MortonFranksWilliams.MFWWitness","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Knot.MortonFranksWilliams.MFWWitness","kind":"structure","line":69,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Knot/MortonFranksWilliams.lean#L69-L91","doc":"The MFW input for one braid representative: `n` strands, writhe `e`, and\nthe `v`-degree window `[dmin, dmax]` of the link's HOMFLY polynomial, together\nwith **the two MFW inequalities as hypotheses**. Nothing here is proved; see\nthe module docstring. ","signatureChunk":0}]}